{"byteLength":902,"contentHash":{"algorithm":"sha256","value":"ce2b2897aa363b5e6b1d2443dc165ae1a695b63aa6cf6e39904fd2e9356b33b4"},"kind":"skillDocument","name":"references/stdlib/NetworkErrorKind.md","producer":{"build":{"commit":"5de2594ad523fba4f38fa63f7a1b306e8a23eb0c","dirty":false,"provenance":{"commit":"git","dirty":"environment"},"target":"aarch64-apple-darwin"},"name":"benitoite","version":"0.0.13"},"schemaVersion":1,"text":"# Benitoite.NetworkErrorKind\n\nStatus: standard, in the prelude. It can be used without `import`.\n\nRefer to its declarations as `NetworkErrorKind.<name>`, for example `NetworkErrorKind.NetworkErrorKind`.\n\nKinds of network failures.\n\n```benitoite\n@extensible\npublic data NetworkErrorKind\n  /// The name cannot be resolved.\n  HostNotFound\n  /// The connection was refused.\n  ConnectionRefused\n  /// The connection was cut in the middle.\n  ConnectionReset\n  /// The time ran out.\n  TimedOut\n  /// The address and port to listen on are in use.\n  AddressInUse\n  /// What was received is not valid HTTP.\n  InvalidHTTPData\n  /// A URL or an address is not in a valid form.\n  InvalidInput\n  /// The operating system refused the operation.\n  PermissionDenied\n  /// None of the above, including a failed TLS certificate check.\n  Other\nend data\n```\n\nThe kind of a network failure, returned by `NetworkError.kind`.\n"}
